            {
              "line": 1,
              "text": "# HYPIC: Accelerating Hybrid-Attention LLM Serving with Position-Independent Caching"
            },
            {
              "line": 5,
              "text": "HYPIC is the first serving system to bring position-independent caching (PIC) to hybrid-attention LLMs. Existing PIC reuses per-token KV cache, but hybrid stacks are mostly linear-attention layers that expose only a per-request recurrent st"
            },
            {
              "line": 13,
              "text": "Across four hybrid-attention models and five workloads, HYPIC cuts TTFT by **3.25\u00d7** and lifts QPS by **1.66\u00d7** over Prefix Cache, within **1.71** points of Full Recompute. Built on [SGLang](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang) v0.5.14. S"
            },
            {
              "line": 18,
              "text": "git clone https://github.com/redai-infra/HYPIC.git && cd HYPIC"
            },
            {
              "line": 24,
              "text": "Enable PIC on any launch by adding the PIC flags. Prompts are split into"
            },
            {
              "line": 25,
              "text": "reusable segments at a separator string (`<<PIC_SEP>>`):"
            },
            {
              "line": 33,
              "text": "  --pic-separator-str '<<PIC_SEP>>' \\"
            },
            {
              "line": 47,
              "text": "  \"text\": \"You are a helpful assistant.<<PIC_SEP>>The Eiffel Tower is in Paris, France.<<PIC_SEP>>Mount Fuji is the tallest mountain in Japan.<<PIC_SEP>>Question: In which country is the Eiffel Tower?\","
            },
            {
              "line": 52,
              "text": "Each `<<PIC_SEP>>`-delimited chunk is cached position-independently and reused across requests regardless of order. "
            },
            {
              "line": 59,
              "text": "| `quick_test_offline.py` | 6-way in-process (`sgl.Engine`) comparison \u2014 full_recompute / prefix_cache / pic_addition / pic_transition / pic_transition_rope / pic_transition_rope_recompute \u2014 on one model. |"
            },
            {
              "line": 61,
              "text": "| `diag_layer_divergence.py` | Per-layer bisect: finds the first decoder layer where PIC's residual diverges from the baseline (accuracy debugging). |"
            },
            {
              "line": 62,
              "text": "| `distribute/` | Segment parallelism \u2014 4-prefill + 1-decode PIC scatter cluster, with an LPT-vs-RR speedup/correctness harness. See `examples/pic/distribute/README.md`. |"
            },
            {
              "line": 69,
              "text": "# per-layer divergence bisect (PIC vs baseline)"
            },
            {
              "line": 70,
              "text": "PIC_DIAG_MODE=transition_rope python examples/pic/diag_layer_divergence.py"
            },
            {
              "line": 74,
              "text": "export DISTPIC_UCX_ENV=\"UCX_NET_DEVICES=mlx5_1:1,... UCX_IB_GID_INDEX=7\"  # required on RDMA/IB hosts (see distribute/README.md)"
            },
            {
              "line": 75,
              "text": "bash cluster.sh up          # 4 prefill + 1 decode + single-GPU PIC baseline (boots in background)"
            },
            {
              "line": 83,
              "text": "model path / TP with `PIC_MODEL` / `PIC_TP`."
            },
            {
              "line": 85,
              "text": "## PIC modes"
            },
            {
              "line": 91,
              "text": "| `addition` | segment state add      | no               | no | naive linear-attention PIC baseline.                          |"
            },
            {
              "line": 92,
              "text": "| `transition` | cached transition operator | no              | no | Core HYPIC state compose.                                     |"
            },
            {
              "line": 96,
              "text": "The seam width is a runtime knob independent of mode: `PIC_SEAM_SINK`"
            },
            {
              "line": 115,
              "text": "  title={HYPIC: Accelerating Hybrid-Attention LLM Serving with Position-Independent Caching},"
            }
